      "side": 1,
      "message": "Although I can eventually figure out what you mean by the two separate types of versions (p.properties.Srcs_version distinct from p.versionsSupported), it seems to me that it\u0027d be even better if we can clarify the distinctions upfront with enums or something like that. I think we\u0027d also want a separate method that does the parsing to clarify what\u0027s going on. Something similar to (but more complete than) :\n\nfunc parseSupportedVersions(input interface{}) {\n  myString, ok :\u003d input.(string)\n  if ok {\n    if myString \u003d\u003d \"\" {\n      return defaultInterpreterVersions\n    }\n    if myString \u003d\u003d \"ALL\" {\n      return [\"PY2\", \"PY3\"]\n    }\n    return parseSupportedVersions([myString])\n  }\n  results \u003d []\n  for _, item :\u003d range input {\n    switch item {\n      case \"PY2\":\n      results \u003d append(results, interpreterPy2)\n      case \"PY3\":\n      results \u003d append(results, interpreterPy2)\n    }\n  }\n  return results  \n}\n\n\n(the exact details will probably depend on what we do about the p.properties.Srcs_version discussion on line 45)",
